      "writtenOn": "2019-11-13T17:24:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the delayed responce, I finally took a swing at this last friday, and am starting to look at it again. Unfortunately I\u0027m missing something as trying to use clk_get from the provider driver seems problematic, as I have the clk name, but clk_get wants a the indirect clk id name (so instead of the specific \"gcc_disp_axi_clk\" it looks for \"ref\" or whatever the indirect name is in the dt). \n\nIs there a better interface to get the proper handle to enable in the provider driver?",
      "parentUuid": "715a53dd_61bd0cb5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3617,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 3617,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "281e030049d200dc00db29642b4f0a079eeb2555",
