      "writtenOn": "2019-11-13T22:25:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the quick feedback!\n\nHrm. The clks/clocks-name bits in the clockprovider seems a little sketchy (the bindings for that might be a tough sell upstream). Are you suggesting a separate dummy driver instead?\n\nI just took a swing trying to use my own references and do something like clk_core_prepare_enable() on the clk_hw core but that function isn\u0027t exported. So I\u0027m still fishing around for a path.\n\nI\u0027d be happy to checkout and play with your approach, just let me know!",
      "parentUuid": "8f727d25_408c0147",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3617,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 3617,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "281e030049d200dc00db29642b4f0a079eeb2555",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c89d8a41_13d7c3c5",
        "filename": "drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sdm845.c",
